{
  "about": [
    "Questions people ask, the tool call a good answer makes, and checks on the structured result.",
    "Run the checks: LER_DB=../lers_analysis.db cargo test evals -- --ignored --nocapture",
    "Manual check in Claude: ask `question` and see whether it makes a call like `call`.",
    "Paths are JSON pointers into structured_content; a `*` segment means every array element.",
    "ops: eq, contains (string or array), one_of, min, max, len, len_min, error_contains.",
    "Counts are ranges so a data refresh doesn't break them; tighten them after a deliberate change."
  ],
  "cases": [
    {
      "id": "last-5-sequoyah",
      "question": "Give me the last 5 LERs from Sequoyah",
      "call": {
        "tool": "search_events",
        "args": {
          "plant": "Sequoyah",
          "limit": 5
        }
      },
      "checks": [
        {
          "path": "/results",
          "op": "len",
          "value": 5
        },
        {
          "path": "/results/*/site",
          "op": "eq",
          "value": "Sequoyah"
        },
        {
          "path": "/total",
          "op": "min",
          "value": 100
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "misspelled-plant",
      "question": "last 5 events at seqouah",
      "call": {
        "tool": "search_events",
        "args": {
          "plant": "seqouah",
          "limit": 5
        }
      },
      "checks": [
        {
          "path": "/notes/0",
          "op": "contains",
          "value": "Sequoyah"
        },
        {
          "path": "/results/*/site",
          "op": "eq",
          "value": "Sequoyah"
        }
      ]
    },
